.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox-dkms 1  "garuda-toolbox 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-dkms \- Show and build the DKMS modules of each kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox dkms\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show and build the DKMS modules of each kernel
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-dkms\-list(1)
The modules DKMS builds and the kernels each is built for
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-dkms\-build(1)
Build every module a kernel lacks, or the ones of one kernel
.SH EXTRA
Example:
  garuda\-toolbox dkms build
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox(1)
